@flexiarg pattern-interpretation/compile-guards-exactly
@title Compile Guards Exactly, Including Unknowns And Disjunctions
@keywords guard, strong-Kleene, NNF, DNF, siblings, add-only, split-THEN
@audience cascade-model builders, admission gates
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; design PROPOSAL-pattern-interpretation D2-D5 by claude-4, not yet approved; checked against futon2 find_receipt/guard-value and receipt_construction/acting-order; F4 split agreed by claude-4)
@references [pattern-interpretation/declare-the-universe pattern-interpretation/reproduce-the-recorded-run translation/choose-the-equivalence-check contracts/declare-the-reductions]
@see-also hygiene/receipt-then-gate
@why the model's state is a set of tokens and enactment evaluates guards in three-valued (strong Kleene) logic over a fact map. If the encoding treats a missing token as false, the model fires a pattern enactment would not, and prediction and enactment disagree exactly on unobserved facts.
@how each fact f gives two tokens, f⁺ (established) and f⁻ (observed false); q0 holds f⁺ for true, f⁻ for false and neither for :unknown. Put the guard in negation normal form and expand to a disjunction of conjunctions; each conjunction becomes a sibling pattern in the same precedence slot, where [:fact f] requires f⁺ and [:not [:fact f]] requires f⁻ and forbids f⁺ (guards never remove tokens; states only gain them). Effects produce f⁺ only (add-only; retraction refused). An effect that would produce f⁺ where f⁻ is already observed leaves both tokens, a state no enactment can reach, and is refused at admission as a typed conflict; the remedy is to express the change as a new positive fact (…-observes-cleanly rather than retracting …-throws). A THEN holding two acts is split into consecutive parts p#1, p#2 carrying :source-pattern and :part, the second's guard requiring the first's token. A check's pass or fail enters by observation, not as an effect.
@violation-signature a missing token read as false (the wired tick lane on 2026-09-16, p4ng vm/tick-001/12-R9-wiring.edn: facts {:a true :b :unknown}, guard forbidding b, the lane's enactment plan fired [:p] where live acting-order returns []); an effect producing f⁺ over an observed f⁻ admitted; an :or guard refused, dropping a real interpretation; a false effect accepted; two acts compiled as one effect; "refused" modelled as a produced token.
! conclusion: Two tokens per fact, sibling expansion for disjunctions, add-only effects without f⁺/f⁻ conflicts and linked parts for multi-act THENs make the compiled guard fire exactly when strong-Kleene enactment does on observed states; on predicted states there is no enactment to compare, and the encoding is the definition.

  + context: Prediction (B, rollout, G) and enactment (acting-order) consume the same interpretation.

  + IF:
    An admitted guard and effect must become a token kernel.

  + HOWEVER:
    Closed-world token sets and three-valued guards disagree on unknowns; disjunctions and multi-act THENs have no single-pattern encoding.

  + THEN:
    Use the two-token encoding, sibling expansion and linked parts.

  + BECAUSE:
    NNF and distribution are valid in strong Kleene logic, so the siblings are enabled exactly when the guard is true.

  + evidence: R9's wired-tick finding above (unknown read as false); worked example agent/evidence-over-assertion (PROPOSAL §4); inbox-zero NOT(tests-exist AND tests-pass) sibling check; receipt-then-gate split (F4); test-registry check outcome as observation (F11).
